    "turn_text": "Today's podcast is sponsored by Healthy Cell. Reach your potential. Get 20% off your first order with code CARTER that's C-A-R-T-E-R at HealthyCell.com. Backslash Carter, Healthy Cell. It makes me feel great. Today we've got Arizona Congressman Andy Biggs on the show with us. He is not only a great representative and has fought diligently for our country specifically when we think of our border issues, but he is a good friend. And I am grateful to have him on the show today. He'll join me. He's going to be discussing that stunning leak from the SCOTUS, from the Supreme Court of the draft opinions regarding the overturning of Roe versus Wade and Casey. This is so important because I'm actually here covering the story in Virginia right now. That's why I'm here at the beautiful studios here in Radio America and Arlington. I'm not in Texas, I'm not on the border, but I will talk to you about what I experienced in Judge Alito's neighborhood with the group of protesters, about 100 roughly protesters that marched through that neighborhood. And I gotta tell you, it still is leaving me stunned. the things that I heard are, for me, I mean, really tore up my soul. I could not believe what I was hearing from the women that were there. The pro-abortion activists, that's what I'm gonna call them, pro-abortion activists. This isn't about pro-choice. I didn't hear any relevant arguments. What I heard was actually, it made it seem as though the insane were running the asylum and I felt devastated to hear some of the things I heard there. It was very disturbing. Later, I also have news on the show about UFOs, unidentified flying objects, or as they like to say it now, unidentified aerial phenomena. This is not something from the Twilight Zone, guys. This is reality. The Senate is holding hearings on this. There is a lot of concern. This is a bipartisan effort in the Senate to find out what is happening in our skies and what we cannot identify. There are objects in our skies that appear to be moving at speeds that we could not possibly have here on Earth. There are issues associated with that, that Senator Kirsten Gillibrand, she's a Democrat from New York, and others here on the ground, Senator Marco Rubio, also on the House Intelligence Committee in Florida, are very interested in and want to investigate. So we're going to talk about that and so much, so much, so much more. Please follow and subscribe. I'd like you to get all the links at Sarah A Carter dot com. That is Sarah A Carter dot com. Okay. Don't go to Sarah Carter dot com unless you want to buy some paintings. But you throw the A in there and you'll go to my website. We have all the latest stories, all of the links to all my social media. And you can also get on my email list once you're there. And once you sign up for the email list, you will not get shadow band. promise you that we'll be able to stay in touch no matter what happens. Obviously, we have a lot of faith right now on Twitter with Elon Musk and he's been making some pretty important statements and some great statements. But I think we still have to be very cautious about what's happening. This is an election year and there can be many significant changes. And we're going to be talking about that with the congressman as well. Congressman Andy Biggs is coming up on the show. You do not want to miss him. You do not want to miss him. We're going to be talking about everything and the things that are most important to you, SCOTUS decision, overturning Roe versus Wade, the border and everything else. Before I get to Congressman Biggs, I want to talk to you about a sponsor for our show that I absolutely believe in. A group that I believe fights for freedom, fights for our country, fights for the basic principles that make us so great and that's AMAC. That's AMAC, guys. The Association of Mature American Citizens. And by the way, you don't need to be 50 plus to join AMAC. AMAC will fight the good fight for you. They take it right here to Capitol Hill, into the swamp, and they battle it out. And they go to Capitol Hill, they talk to congressional members. And I'm going to tell you, it's a company that I absolutely, an organization, I absolutely believe in. They believe in fighting the good fight against reckless government spending. the ever expanding scope of the federal government, helping small businesses, securing our borders. I mean, this is everything we talk about all the time anyways, supporting our military and respecting our veterans. They believe in standing before the flag and the kneeling before God. by joining AMAT, you're taking the first steps to saving the America you love. AMAC offers an alternative to just about every other benefit that that other group offers. But guess what, guys, without the liberal agenda, I stand with AMAC and I hope that you will too. Thank you. So I'm going to start with coming into Virginia to cover SCOTUS. The outrageous, unbelievable leaking of the draft opinions of our Supreme Court justices regarding Roe vs. Wade. Something that has never, ever been done in the history of the SCOTUS, right? This is like a trampling on the sacred ground of our country. We have, you know, branches of government. And we respect those divisions and those lines. But obviously somebody, a clerk or someone within the scotus, and we better find out who that is. But by the way, most of the time we never find out who leakers are, right? Remember what happened to President Trump when people were going through his phone calls and leaking those phone calls to the media? Remember what happened there? Nothing. They never caught the people that they should have caught. There's never punishment here in Washington, D.C. For some of these, some of these people that believe they are above the law, some of these people who believe they know what's best for you and I, right? So they leaked the draft opinions. By the way, I read Justice Alito's draft opinion a couple of times, actually, because it's so brilliant. Alito's draft opinion, 98 pages, I believe, just completely brilliant arguments. And even on my flight into Virginia from Texas, I believed that I should review it again because he lays out these incredible arguments of why this issue of abortion should go back to the states because we are a republic. We are a republic and Roe versus Wade was based on faulty assumptions and he lays it out. He lays it out. You know, abortion was not a historical right in this country. It wasn't something that we had embedded in our constitution. It's not, it's something that should be left up to the states. So if you're, if you're thinking you only know about like Roe versus Wade is being overturned, we're going to lose our ability to have an abortion for those of you that believe in that. That's not the case. What the justices are saying is that they cannot legislate the law. It should have never happened from the beginning, that every individual state and its constituents in those states, its residents, have the right to dictate how the state handles that. That was based on a case in Mississippi that was brought before the Supreme Court, where in Mississippi, it was like 15 weeks or later, no abortion. And this is the reason why and here are the facts as we have laid them out. And if you want to real, if you want to just keep an open mind, read Justice Alito's argument. It's out there. It's leaked. We already know it. What we don't know is the final drafts. Those have not been issued. Those have not yet been issued by the courts. We do know that Alito, Kavanaugh, Barrett, all of them are now probably in hiding somewhere. And I've spoken to a couple of sources who have said, yes, they have left their homes. They're in undisclosed locations and that, you know, they are very, very concerned for the safety of themselves and their families. So I came here. Last night on a very last minute flight went straight from the airport, straight over to Justice Alito's neighborhood. Apparently he was not home nor his family, but a group of maybe about 100 plus people came marching down the streets. And it was mostly women, there were men there, and I just couldn't believe what I was hearing. I couldn't believe what I was seeing. You know, regardless of how any of us feel about the issue of abortion and the complex nature of that argument, right, when you hear people say, well, what if it's a 12-year-old girl? What if it's a 10-year-old girl? What if it's somebody who's been raped by a family member? What if it's this? What if it's that? What if it's the life of the mom? Regardless of the argument, regardless of the argument, it is a human life. And I've always believed, and I consider myself a very spiritual person, somebody who prays quite often goes to church as much as I can, but absolutely believes there is a God. But even if I didn't, it's a human life. that shouldn't be easy, that shouldn't be something you smile or laugh about, that shouldn't be something that you joke around about, that is a child, a potential life that exists that could have the opportunity to experience all the most wonderful things that we get to experience, even in moments where it's sad, right? Even when life isn't perfect and it shouldn't be. We experience it. We experience this great miracle of life. So you would think like no matter what, we should do that, right? I heard women say things like they wish they had been aborted. women saying things that joking around about it, saying they're going to have a, you know, they're going to have a celebration for the next person's abortion, telling people don't forget, don't miss your appointment at the abortion clinic. It's going to be awesome and we're going to throw you a party. I just felt like the crazies were running the institutions. I felt like I was surrounded by people who had no love left in them or very little and people that were so extreme, so destroyed by something that they had turned into this kind of like chaos of evil. I don't even understand what was going on there. It was very, very disturbing to me. Very disturbing to me. I'm gonna play this clip. This is MSNBC panelist and comedian Lori Kilmartin. I couldn't even believe this when I heard this. She says she wants to have sex with whoever leaked the draft opinion and then abort the baby. Take a listen to this.",
