    "turn_text": "Yeah, no. I mean, there's no accountability. We don't have a pay for it. We don't say, well, we're going to pay for it by doing X and Y. We're giving them stingers and javelin missiles, not out of our surplus, but out of our stockpile. It takes almost three years to make a single missile like that. And so we're decreasing our readiness, supplying Ukraine, and a million bucks a copy. uh, at least. And so you just go, well, well, what, what is the end game? I mean, I mean, we're dealing with people who would like to sit around an academic salon at a university and just gab about, well, you know, multilateral institutionalism, neoliberal institutional, that's the way to do it. But the rest of the world's dictators, they think in the terms of realism. And the term of realism is power. It's all about power. And they say, well, hey, you know what? Hey, we just got a break. The crazy cowboy Donald Trump, he's not in charge anymore. So we can just base, you got this guy who's a lame-o from some Jerry Lewis movie. Joe Biden, who's wandering around, he's looking for an ice cream sandwich on the White House lawn. The Easter bunnies is chief communications director. They can do what they want because we don't project, we don't even project strength anymore.",
