    "turn_file": "/shared/3/projects/podcasts/transcriptionQueue/turns/pol_appearance_episodes_interviews/8/6/86166.jsonl",
    "turn_idx": 72,
    "turn_text": "Well, I mean, I look back and I remember Tip O'Neill, who was Speaker of the House, very left, you know, old-line Democrat and Ronald Reagan, they used to, you know, Ronald Reagan, if you read his one of his biographies, he says, oh, you know, I hadn't tipped over to the White House for dinner, we sat around, we ate on TV trays, they'd eat on TV trays, Tip O'Neill takes his shoes off, he's sitting there, and they have this great conversation, they're laughing and scratching and all that stuff. And then the next day, Tip O'Neill goes out and just beats the crud out of Ronald Reagan again. And Reagan calls it up and says, hey, what's the deal? And he says, well, hey, when I'm working, I'm going to beat the tar out of you, but we can get together after hours and have a good time. We can go for the exam. I mean, that's really kind of the way it is. That's the way it should be. It's not that way anymore. You know, after January 6, 2021. People I've been working on who co-sponsored my legislation and that I, on the other side, and I co-sponsored their legislation after January 6th. These people wouldn't even talk to me. I'm like, I did the same thing you did four years ago. What is going on here? I'm afraid that it's just the chasm between both sides is so great now that it takes a little bit to break through. I mean, I broke through with one of my bills. uh, called the Prada bill, which is a Puerto Rican accountability bill for all the bail out money, uh, transparency, right? You know, it got passed into law. I was a lead Republican. We had a Democrat on the other side. But we were able to do that. But, you know, right to try. We crossed the aisle. Kirsten, a cinema. And I, we were able to bridge the gap on that. But so much of this is so personal. I don't, I usually don't, I really don't try not to take any of this stuff personally. But I figure people just hate me. That's okay. That's, that's the frog in a painting. But you know what?",
    "speaker_id": "SPEAKER_02",
