    "turn_file": "/shared/3/projects/podcasts/transcriptionQueue/turns/pol_appearance_episodes_interviews/8/6/86166.jsonl",
    "turn_idx": 95,
    "turn_text": "You all know how much I love my pillow. I talk about it. I have my pillow for my dogs. I've got like four dog beds in my house. They're all my pillow. I have my pillow sheets, my pillow towel sets, my pillow pillows. I just, I love it. I love the fact that it's an American company. It's run by a great patriot, Mike Lindell, who I consider a friend. And I think you all too. You want to support American companies. This is why I have my pillow as a sponsor for my show. Well, right now, There is a BOGO extravaganza. I mean, it's huge. You're talking my pillow bed sheets as low as $59.98, elegance my pillow as low as $49.98, roll and go anywhere my pillows for $29.98, and there is so much more guys, so much more. Roll and go anywhere my pillow. Use it on your couch, your recliner, in your car. I mean, I can't even begin to tell you what a cool product this is. It's versatile enough. that you can take it with you on vacation anywhere you go. And I'm going to be taking it with me on our vacation coming up soon, available in multiple colors and patterns. It's machine washable and dryable. You don't even have to worry about that and it's got a 10 year warranty. You just can't beat that with a money back guarantee. You'll have a 60 day money back guarantee if you don't like it, okay? So it's a buy one, get one extravaganza at MyPillow.com backslashcarder. You get bed sheets and pillows. They're just the tip of the iceberg. Find the full list of BOGO offers by visiting MyPillow.com backslashcarder or call 1-800-685-7221. Stock up with the buy one, get one free savings today and get Mike's book. Listen to this, Mike's book free with any purchase. MyPillow.com backslash Carter or call 1-800-68-57221. MyPillow.com backslash Carter. Okay, so I did talk to Congressman Biggs a little bit about UFOs. It makes him a little uncomfortable. That's fine. Not everybody is comfortable discussing this subject. Why? Because it is something that we've never been allowed to discuss before. You know, I've had Lou Elizondo on the show many times. I've had Nick Pope on the show. All of these are familiar names with those of you who are familiar with unidentified aerial phenomena or UFOs. Nick Pope, who worked with the British government, he was the top guy for the British Defense Ministry's press and was very familiar with reporting sightings of UFOs, both on the military level as well as the civilian commercial aircraft, and Lou Elizondo, who I consider a great friend, a good friend. who worked at the Pentagon at their ATIP program. He was the director there studying UFOs. Well, it's a very big deal right now in the Senate as well as in the House. The information that has been released publicly just over the past few years, the videos of objects flying in the sky. Literally moving 700 to 900 G's. Just so you all understand this, the human body can only really withstand, I think it's about seven to nine G's. So imagine an object moving 700 to 900 G's. It appears here and then it appears there. instantaneously, you know, right before the eyes of our fighter pilots in our military, which is what you heard at the top of this segment. It is absolutely stunning, the kind of advancements our technology has allowed us to have that we can spot these unidentified aerial phenomena or UFOs in our skies. Now, Does it mean that these are from aliens from another planet? No, we don't really understand what we're seeing here. We don't really understand. That's why the US Senate has been receiving classified briefings from the intelligence community as well as the Pentagon over the past few weeks. Yeah, it's just happening right now. and the New York Times is reporting and others are reporting that the House Subcommittee is actually scheduled to hold next week the first open congressional hearing on unidentified aerial vehicles in more than half a century. Although I'm going to tell you, I actually attended and I don't understand I don't understand how they're saying this, but there was a testimony that was given under the Bush administration before Congress. So I'm going to have to look that up and talk to you guys about that because I did cover that story. And I believe it was back in 2010 or 2009 here in Washington DC. when they were supposed to be releasing information disclosure. So we've got to be really careful because there's a lot of people that want to keep whatever's going on in our skies a secret. I'm grateful that we're having this committee hearing. It's going to be very interesting to hear what comes out. This is from the New York Times. The hearing comes after a release last June of a report requested by Congress on unidentified aerial phenomena, the nine-page preliminary assessment, which I considered kind of bogus. I didn't think it went deep enough, and I thought it was just kind of like they wanted to whitewash everything, right? From the Office of the Director of National Intelligence focused on 144 incidents, incidents, sightings dating back to 2004. So I want you to know that these incidents were similar ones were also reported going all the way back to the 1940s and 1930s, even before that, similar incidences. These were the 144 incidents, mainly our military picked up. And there was evidence of it in actual like satellite imagery that they could pick up in radar. So that go back to 2004, the report declined, however, to draw inferences, saying that the available reporting was largely inconclusive and noting that limited and inconsistent data created a challenge on evaluating the phenomena. But it said most of the phenomena reported do represent physical objects. Guys, if there is stuff in our skies flying around our nuclear facilities and around our naval warships and our F-18 hornets, And they are moving 700 to 900 G's. We better hell know what's going on in our skies. We don't know if it's from another planet. We don't know if it's from another universe. I don't know. We don't know. We just don't know because our technology doesn't have that kind of capability that we know of. And I've been talking to lots of folks and go back and listen to some of the podcasts with Lou Elizondo with Nick Pope, you're gonna be stunned at what they say to you. I mean, you're gonna get a better idea of this, right? But now we know we're gonna have these hearings. I'm gonna keep you posted on these hearings. I'm gonna be bringing experts on to discuss this. Hopefully we'll bring Lou back on as well to talk about this. And let's see if we can get some of those senators on the show as well to talk about what could possibly be happening, why, Is this such a critical juncture in our time of humanity? Why we need to understand this? And could this pose a real threat to our safety and to our world? Again, thank you so much for being a part of the Sarah Carter show. I love having This moment to talk with you, it's just great. I loved having Congressman Andy Biggs on the show. I hope to bring him back on. He's a great American, a great patriot, and he's a great warrior for life. For all those babies out there, we are fighting for you, even though you don't know it. God bless our country. God bless our great nation and help us heal because you guys, we really need all the prayers we can out there. Let's all stick together. Let's all be kind to one another. And I'll see you real soon next week. This is Sarah Carter with the Sarah Carter Show. Go to my website, Sarahacarter.com. Sarahacarter.com where you get all my links and you can sign up for our email list. See you Thursday. I'm so happy to have Kevin to merit here on the Sarah Carter show. He is the founder of Lear Capital. I'm sure you've heard of Lear Capital. I saw a stat that blew me away and it was that over the past 20 years and it's that gold has literally outperformed the S&P 500. Why doesn't everybody know that?",
